@id=still-to-come-is-marked-where-it-is-written @kind=decision
Feature: What is still to come is marked where it is written, and what is built is live and stays so

  Not a folder for work still to come beside one for built work, nor a change kept in a file of its
  own until it is merged into its feature: a feature or a rule still to come declares a maturity
  where it is written, and one that declares none is live, a test that `sdp check` holds to the git
  base, so that nothing live goes back to work still to come without an error. A folder holds one
  dimension well, lifecycle is the one that changes fastest, and a rule is the unit that is built.
  The price is that a feature's file holds live rules and rules still to come, told apart only by
  their tags, that removing what is live takes a rule that replaces it, and that the guarantee holds
  only where git has a base to compare with.
